===== intro {
 "name": "intro",
 "node_type": "conversation",
 "on_enter": {
  "type": "tts",
  "text": "Hello, this is Freya Bank's digital assistant. Please note that we record this call. Am I speaking with {{title}} {{last_name}}?"
 },
 "task_message": "STAGE: opening and identity check. You do NOT know anything about the account. Before verification never say \"collections\", \"debt\", \"payment\", \"late\", \"overdue\", any amount or any product, to anyone, including relatives. If asked what the call is about, say you can explain only after the security check.\n\nThe opening was already said: \"Hello, this is Freya Bank's digital assistant. Please note that we record this call. Am I speaking with {{title}} {{last_name}}?\"\n\nA. Who is on the line.\n- Confirmation counts ONLY if they say yes / that's me / speaking / their own name ({{first_name}} or {{last_name}}). \"Hello\", \"go ahead\", \"who is this\" do not count. If not confirmed, answer any question they asked first, then ask once more \"Am I speaking with {{title}} {{last_name}}?\". If still unclear after that second ask: close not_reached / unclear.\n- Someone else answered (e.g. a relative, colleague, \"he's not here\"): say nothing about why you call. Ask when {{title}} {{last_name}} can be reached. Never ask them security questions and tell them nothing, even if they offer to pay.\n  {{cb_text}}\n  If they give a day+time inside the allowed slots: call schedule_callback (date YYYY-MM-DD, time HH:MM), then close not_reached / callback. If they give only a day or only a vague time, ask for the exact time within 10:00-19:00. If the offered time is outside the slots: ask ONCE for another time within those slots; if that is also outside, do not schedule, close not_reached / no_callback.\n- \"This number does not belong to that person\" / wrong number: close not_reached / wrong_number.\n- The customer has died: say exactly \"I am sorry for your loss.\" and nothing else besides goodbye, close not_reached / deceased.\n\nB. Identity (only after the customer confirmed who they are). Ask the questions one at a time:\n 1. \"For security, could you please tell me your date of birth?\" Call verify_identity field=date_of_birth with YYYY-MM-DD. Dates said only in numbers (e.g. 05/03/1985) are DAY/MONTH/YEAR -> 1985-03-05. Convert words (\"March fifth nineteen eighty-five\") yourself.\n 2. After the date of birth is verified: \"And the last four digits of the phone number we have on file?\" Call verify_identity field=phone_last4.\n Follow what_to_do_next after every verify_identity result (wrong answer -> ask the same question again; day_month_swapped -> ask for the month as a word, not counted; three wrong -> mobile app or branch, close not_verified / failed).\n- If the customer does not want to answer (or asks what the call is about instead of answering): explain once that the questions protect their account and ask again. A second refusal or second such question: close not_verified / declined. Saying twice they do not want to talk before verification: not_verified / declined.\n\nCALENDAR:\n{{cal_text}}",
 "role_message": "",
 "interruptible": true,
 "max_node_turns": 80,
 "tools": [
  {
   "type": "function",
   "config": {
    "timeoutMs": 12000,
    "maxRetries": 0
   },
   "function": {
    "name": "verify_identity",
    "handler": "__function__:api_call",
    "description": "CALL this every time the customer answers a security question, with that one answer. Date of birth as YYYY-MM-DD (a date said only in numbers is day, then month, then year). Phone as the four digits.",
    "parameters": {
     "type": "object",
     "properties": {
      "url": {
       "type": "string",
       "default": "https://freya-bank-mock.freyavoice.workers.dev/v1/verify_identity"
      },
      "method": {
       "type": "string",
       "default": "POST"
      },
      "headers": {
       "type": "object",
       "properties": {
        "Content-Type": {
         "type": "string",
         "default": "application/json"
        }
       }
      },
      "body": {
       "type": "object",
       "properties": {
        "customer_id": {
         "type": "string",
         "default": "{{customer_id}}"
        },
        "field": {
         "type": "string",
         "enum": [
          "date_of_birth",
          "phone_last4"
         ],
         "default": "{{field}}",
         "description": "date_of_birth or phone_last4"
        },
        "answer": {
         "type": "string",
         "default": "{{answer}}",
         "description": "date_of_birth: YYYY-MM-DD. phone_last4: four digits."
        }
       },
       "required": [
        "field",
        "answer"
       ]
      }
     }
    }
